Description: 
  # ChannelAttribution: Markov Model for Online Multi-Channel Attribution

  ## Purpose

  Advertisers use a variety of online marketing channels to reach consumers and want to know the degree each channel contributes to success. This is the online multi-channel attribution problem. This package implements a probabilistic solution using a k-order Markov model to capture structural correlations in customer-journey data. It also provides three heuristic algorithms (first-touch, last-touch, linear-touch). Core routines are implemented in C++/Cython for performance.

  ## Installation

  ### From PyPI

  ```bash
  pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel
  pip install ChannelAttribution
